IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- INSTRUMENT: the Telecommunications (Cancellation) Notification 2011, G.N. No. S 22/2011, made by the Info-communications Development Authority of Singapore "in exercise of the powers conferred by section 26(5) of the Telecommunications Act"
-- (the section 26 of the Revised Edition 2000, deposited at TA1999.20001230.txt:971-990, runs from (1) to (4) and has no (5); which text of the Act "section 26(5)" reads was not determined).  Made 6 January 2011; first published in the Government Gazette on 17 January 2011 at 5:00 pm; in operation 21 January 2011 (paragraph 1).
-- Deposited 2026-11-04 under subjects/sg/telecommunications-cancellation-notification-2011/registers/source-bundle/ (TA1999-CANC-S22-2011), from the e-Gazette, at an exact URL that the orchestrating session read off a result in the e-Gazette index and passed to the encoder.
-- The independent reviewer found it; it is not among the 40 texts on IMDA's Telecommunications Act page.
--
-- WHAT IT SAYS.  Paragraph 2 cancels thirteen notifications, items (a) to (m).  The titles as the text prints them: items (a) to (f) are exemptions from the Telecom Competition Code, items (g) to (j) exemptions from the Dominant Licensee Provisions in the Telecom Competition Code 2005,
-- item (k) "the Exemption for International Telephone Services Notification 2007", items (l) and (m) exemptions for named services of 2009.  The thirteen notifications are NOT deposited and were NOT searched for by this encoder.
-- They are named by their titles and G.N. numbers in the items below, and nothing in them is encoded here.
--
-- WHY THIS MODULE IS SMALL.  The Notification cancels all thirteen on one day, so there is no table of which notification stood cancelled on which day: from 21 January 2011 all thirteen, and before it none by this Notification.
-- Whether each was itself in operation before that day is a fact of each notification, which is not held.  The module therefore encodes only what the Notification itself says: the day it begins, which notifications it names, and the two-date rule (as for the other instruments of this encoding).
-- The receiver question does not turn on it: the thirteen titles name exemptions from the Competition Code or its Dominant Licensee Provisions, or for named services, and none names a receiver, a broadcast, or any of the provisions of Part 6 the question runs through.
-- The seat modules (sgta-tv-*.l4) do not consult this module.

-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:10 | (CHAPTER 323)
-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:12 | TELECOMMUNICATIONS
-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:13 | (CANCELLATION)
-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:14 | NOTIFICATION 2011
-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:16 | ARRANGEMENT OF PARAGRAPHS
-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:18 | Paragraph
-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:19 | 1. Citation and commencement
-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:20 | 2. Cancellation
-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:24 | In exercise of the powers conferred by section 26(5) of the
-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:25 | Telecommunications Act, the Info-communications Development
-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:26 | Authority of Singapore hereby makes the following Notification:
-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:28 | Citation and commencement
-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:29 | 1. This Notification may be cited as the Telecommunications
-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:30 | (Cancellation) Notification 2011 and shall come into operation on
-- src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:31 | 21st January 2011.
@ref S 22/2011: enacting words and paragraph 1 (citation and commencement) (src:TA1999-CANC-S22-2011:10-31)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 22/2011 para 1: the Notification is in operation on the date (from 21 January 2011)` MEANS d AT LEAST (Date 21 1 2011)

